{"content":{"result":[{"rank_order":1,"title":"Amazon Bedrock expands support for Service Quotas - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a managed service for enterprise-grade access to high-performing foundation models from leading AI companies, now supports viewing inference quotas for the bedrock-mantle endpoint through AWS Service Quotas. This allows customers to track limits for the endpoint in a familiar way and gain visibility into the limits that apply to their workloads. The bedrock-mantle endpoint supports OpenAI Responses API, OpenAI Chat Completions API, and Anthropic Messages API, enabling customers to run existing OpenAI or Anthropic based applications on Amazon Bedrock with minimal code changes. AWS Service Quotas now exposes per-model input-tokens-per-minute and output-tokens-per-minute quotas for supported models on the endpoint. Customers can view their current quotas by opening the AWS Service Quotas console, choosing Amazon Bedrock, and searching for \"Bedrock Mantle\". To request an increase to any quotas, follow the standard Amazon Bedrock limit increase process. Service Quotas support for the bedrock-mantle endpoint is available in all AWS Regions where the endpoint is offered, including US East (N. Virginia, Ohio), US West (Oregon), Asia Pacific (Mumbai, Tokyo, Sydney, Jakarta), Europe (Frankfurt, Ireland, London, Milan, Stockholm), and South America (São Paulo)","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/5/amazon-bedrock-service-quotas/"},{"rank_order":2,"title":"Amazon Bedrock increases default quotas for Anthropic’s Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock, a service offered by AWS, has raised the default quotas for Anthropic's Claude Sonnet 4.5 model in AWS GovCloud (US-West) and AWS GovCloud (US-East) regions. The new quotas are set at 5,000,000 tokens per minute and 1,000 requests per minute, which is a significant 25x increase from the previous limits. This enhancement allows users to efficiently scale their AI workloads in regulated environments. Claude Sonnet 4.5 is Anthropic's latest Sonnet model, known for its proficiency in constructing intricate agents, coding, and long-term tasks while maintaining optimal speed and cost-effectiveness for high-volume applications. To begin using Claude Sonnet 4.5 in Amazon Bedrock, consult the News Blog, AWS GovCloud (US) console, Anthropic's Claude in Amazon Bedrock product page, and the Amazon Bedrock pricing page","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/02/amazon-bedrock-s4.5-quota-aws-govcloud-us/"},{"rank_order":3,"title":"Claude Sonnet 5 is now available on Amazon Bedrock in AWS GovCloud (US) - AWS","context":"AWS GovCloud (US) has added Claude Sonnet 5 to Amazon Bedrock. This model offers strong performance for coding, professional work, and agentic tasks while balancing capability, cost, and speed. For coding, it handles large codebases, multi-file changes, debugging, and refactoring. For agents, it accurately calls tools, maintains state across steps, and recovers from errors. For knowledge work, it constructs spreadsheets, drafts documents, and converts unstructured data into structured analysis.\n\nClaude Opus 4.8 and Claude Sonnet 5 are now accessible on bedrock-runtime endpoints in US-West and US-East regions of AWS GovCloud (US) and bedrock-mantle endpoints in the US-West region. Bedrock Mantle, Amazon Bedrock's next-generation inference engine, supports the Anthropic Messages API. Amazon Bedrock keeps data within AWS infrastructure and offers access to Claude Sonnet 5 through a unified service with managed features like Guardrails, Knowledge Bases, and regional data residency. For more information, refer to the Amazon Bedrock documentation and regional availability","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/07/claude-sonnet-5-govcloud/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"Structured outputs for Claude models available on Amazon Bedrock - AWS","context":"Amazon Bedrock now supports structured outputs for all Anthropic Claude models, enabling schema-compliant JSON responses across both the bedrock-runtime and bedrock-mantle endpoint. This feature allows for automation of reliable tasks in various industries, such as extracting data from financial reports and compliance documents, parsing clinical notes into Electronic Health Records, enriching product catalogs, analyzing contracts, and powering intelligent support ticket routing. The structured outputs are available where Claude models are available, and users can refer to the regional availability details page for more information","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2026/10/claude-structured-outputs-bedrock/"},{"rank_order":5,"title":"amazon-bedrock","skill_description":"Builds generative AI applications on Amazon Bedrock. Covers model invocation (Converse API, InvokeModel), RAG with Knowledge Bases, Bedrock Agents, Guardrails, and AgentCore (including the Harness managed agent loop). Applies when invoking models, setting up or migrating Knowledge Bases to Managed, deploying to AgentCore, migrating/porting/converting a Bedrock Agent (including inline agents) to an AgentCore Harness, troubleshooting Bedrock errors (ThrottlingException, AccessDeniedException), or choosing Bedrock models (Claude, Llama, Nova, Titan). Also for prompt caching, quota and throttling diagnosis, cost tracking, migrating between Claude model generations, chunking strategies, and Bedrock model selection. Covers AgentCore Payments (x402, microtransactions, Payment Manager, Connector, Instrument, Coinbase CDP, Stripe Privy, paid endpoints, agent payments). NOT for custom model training, Rekognition, or Comprehend. For SageMaker model discovery, customization, or endpoints, use aws-ai-ml.\n\nServices: bedrock, bedrock-runtime, bedrock-mantle, bedrock-agent, bedrock-agent-runtime, bedrock-agentcore-control, bedrock-agentcore\nTasks: deploy, debug, optimize, design, migrate\nPersona: developer, devops, architect\nWorkload: generative-ai, rag, agents","skill_name":"amazon-bedrock"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for Claude Sonnet 5 mantle endpoint"}
